WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.667
(intense music)

00:00:04.197 --> 00:00:06.590
(roars)

00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:08.110
- It's Godzilla.

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:10.760
- Well, friends, it is time to
answer the age-old question:

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:13.130
Who would win a fight between a giant ape

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:14.550
and a building-sized lizard?

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:15.860
We're breaking down everything we know

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:19.000
about "Godzilla vs. Kong"
right now on The Ketchup.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.260
On March 31, "Godzilla vs. Kong"

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:23.970
will hit theaters and
HBO Max simultaneously

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:25.750
and we are here for it.

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:27.520
The fourth film in
Legendary's MonsterVerse,

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:31.760
"GVK," as I'm calling it, is
a sequel to 2014's "Godzilla"

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:33.900
as well as "Godzilla:
King of the Monsters"

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.560
and "Kong: Skull Island."

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:36.780
It also marks the first time

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:40.090
these two larger-than-life
leviathans have shared a screen

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:43.040
since 1962's "King Kong vs. Godzilla."

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:45.730
Legendary has armed "Blair
Witch" director Adam Wingard

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:47.384
with a reported $200 million budget,

00:00:47.384 --> 00:00:48.970
and after seeing the trailer,

00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:50.387
we think he put it to good use.

00:00:50.387 --> 00:00:52.499
"Godzilla vs. Kong" looks
like both an epic brawl

00:00:52.499 --> 00:00:55.446
that'll have audiences cheering
for the giant lizard and ape

00:00:55.446 --> 00:00:57.821
and a nail-biting disaster
film for the humans

00:00:57.821 --> 00:01:00.610
unlucky enough to be sitting
ringside to the fight,

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:01.893
which, this time around, includes

00:01:01.893 --> 00:01:04.961
Alexander Skarsgard, Rebecca
Hall, Brian Tyree Henry,

00:01:04.961 --> 00:01:06.256
and returning cast members

00:01:06.256 --> 00:01:08.720
Millie Bobby Brown and Kyle Chandler.

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:11.310
The only question now is who
do you have your money on?

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:12.910
- Kong bows to no one.

00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:16.010
- Updating the franchise for
a new generation of superfans,

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:18.500
Legendary's kaiju are now called titans.

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:20.656
The Godzilla legacy,
meanwhile, sheds its original

00:01:20.656 --> 00:01:23.630
thesis warning about nuclear
capabilities during war

00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:25.180
for a more relevant message

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:27.470
about global warming and eco-terrorism.

00:01:27.470 --> 00:01:29.110
See, in this version of Godzilla,

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:30.648
the radiation emitted by the titans

00:01:30.648 --> 00:01:32.680
is actually healing the planet

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:35.310
and Godzilla, while not
exactly a pro-humanist,

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:38.440
is definitely working to restore
balance in the ecosystem.

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:40.650
Also, there are aliens, as introduced by

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:42.450
the three-headed space dragon Ghidorah

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:43.750
in "King of the Monsters."

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:45.422
Does that explain the tiny spaceship

00:01:45.422 --> 00:01:47.960
next to Kong's inverted
head in the new trailer

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:50.080
or explain where he got his new weapon?

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:52.170
Only time will tell,
but speaking of Kong...

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:53.950
- Is that a monkey?

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:54.856
- We actually don't know that much about

00:01:54.856 --> 00:01:58.170
what Kong has been up to since
we last saw him in the 1970s

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:00.120
in the events of "Kong: Skull Island."

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:01.550
I guess he's just hanging out,

00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:03.410
making friends with small orphan girls

00:02:03.410 --> 00:02:05.700
and chillaxing, if people
still use that word.

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:07.510
But you know, giant gorilla stuff.

00:02:07.510 --> 00:02:09.200
We do know that Monarch,

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:11.540
the government agency working
to understand the titans

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:13.240
in "Godzilla: King of the Monsters,"

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:16.890
was already a shadowy government
organization decades prior

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:18.550
and actively searching for Kong.

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:20.500
We also know from the cave painting scene

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:21.980
in the closing credits of the film

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:24.173
that Kong has tangled with kaiju before,

00:02:24.173 --> 00:02:27.010
including Mothra, Rodan, King Ghidorah,

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:28.850
and, yes, Godzilla himself.

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:30.620
Most importantly, though,
we can see that Kong

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:33.400
had a bit of a growth spurt
since the last time we saw him,

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:34.838
going from roughly 100 feet tall

00:02:34.838 --> 00:02:38.160
to somewhere in the neighborhood
of 300 feet in this film.

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:39.540
Supposedly, that is because Kong

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:41.950
was just an adolescent
the last time we saw him,

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:44.380
and I mean, come on, they
gotta make it a fair fight.

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:45.910
- Let me list all the
ways you're gonna die.

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:47.470
- So, who will win in a fight

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:49.190
between these two mega-predators?

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:51.010
Well, the last time these two met,

00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:53.810
in 1962's "King Kong vs. Godzilla,"

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:55.680
it looked like Godzilla
had the upper hand.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:58.430
I mean, after all, he is
the king of the monsters.

00:02:58.430 --> 00:03:01.210
King Kong, on the other hand,
is just a very large gorilla

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:03.330
who gets sleepy if he
eats too many red berries.

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:04.900
I know the feeling.

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:06.950
After Kong floats to the top of Mount Fuji

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:09.160
on a bunch of balloons -
yup, you heard that right -

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:12.170
he is struck by lightning,
develops his own super powers,

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:15.040
and pummels the amphibious
lizard back into the ocean,

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:16.410
only to resurface alone.

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:20.120
So, Kong wins and it's the end. Or is it?

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:22.460
Hint: It is definitely not the end.

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:24.790
So, does that mean we can expect
to see the king of monsters

00:03:24.790 --> 00:03:27.480
bow down to the king of Kongs yet again?

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:28.730
It's impossible to guess.

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:30.520
Our guess is actually
that the true villains

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:31.880
are probably not either monster,

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:33.400
since they both have vested interests

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:35.040
in protecting at least some of humanity,

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:38.397
not to mention future
franchise installments.

00:03:38.397 --> 00:03:39.418
- [Off Camera] Who bows to who?

00:03:39.418 --> 00:03:40.530
(intense music)

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:43.070
- But friends, it is time for
us to kick it over to you now.

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:46.490
What are your theories
around "Godzilla vs. Kong?"

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:47.830
Let us know in the comments section.

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:50.660
Also let us know who you think
is gonna win this epic brawl.

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:52.388
And of course, if you want
more movie and streaming news,

00:03:52.388 --> 00:03:54.610
head on over to RottenTomatoes.com.

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:56.640
Also, be sure to check
out our show "Versus"

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:58.520
for an even more in-depth breakdown

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:01.030
of Godzilla and Kong
duking it out on screen.

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:03.440
As always, my name's Naz
Perez for Rotten Tomatoes.

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:05.220
We can't thank you enough
for watching The Ketchup

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:06.485
and I got my money on...

00:04:06.485 --> 00:04:08.910
Honestly, I have no idea
who to put my money on.

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:09.790
You tell me.

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:10.623
Bye.

00:04:10.623 --> 00:04:13.096
(upbeat music)

